@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- The nouns of the Income Tax (Rules for Rounding Amounts) Order 5746-1986 and of s 120B(d): DECLARE and nothing else.
-- Kept apart from ito-il30-nouns.l4 so that the Order's two modules (ito-rounding-order-5746.l4, ito-120b-d-rounding-power.l4) can be vendored with this file alone,
-- by a row that needs only the rounding (row IL-03 declines the s 120B amounts for want of it).
-- Sources: ../../registers/source-bundle/regulations/income-tax-rules-for-rounding-amounts-order-5746-1986.he.wiki.txt (sha256 3418c9bd...93b) and the Ordinance,
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt (sha256 b87f2cf4...6b81b6).

§ `Nouns for the Rounding Order`

§§ `The amounts the Rounding Order speaks of (Order ss 1-13) and the amounts it does not`

-- Section 120B(d) lets the Minister of Finance make rules for rounding "amounts adjusted under
-- this section". The Order makes thirteen rules, one per kind of amount (its ss 1-13). Section
-- 120B(a) adjusts five groups of amounts, and the group "social deductions" is a list of
-- fourteen amounts set out in s 120A. Some of those the Order rounds, some it does not name.
-- Each constructor says which section of the Order, or none, speaks to it.
DECLARE `An amount that section 120B adjusts, or that the Rounding Order rounds` IS ONE OF
    `an income ceiling`                                                    -- Order s 1, step 120
    `the amount of a credit point`                                         -- Order s 2, step 12
    `the amount of an allowance point`                                     -- Order s 3, step 1
    `the exemption of a blind or 100% disabled person, section 9(5)(a)`    -- Order s 4, step 1,200
    `the exemption of a blind or disabled person not from personal exertion, section 9(5)(b)` -- Order s 5, step 120
    `a retirement grant or death grant, sections 9(7A) and 32(9)(a)(1)`    -- Order s 6, step 10
    `the discount an employee receives from the employer, section 9(20)`   -- Order s 7, step 12
    `a qualifying annuity, section 9A(a) and (c)`                          -- Order s 8, step 10
    `the exempt amount, section 9A(b)`                                     -- Order s 9, step 1
    `the ceiling for medical-expenses credit, section 44(a)(1)`            -- Order s 10, step 120
    `the amount for credit, section 45A(d)`                                -- Order s 11, step 12
    `qualifying income, section 47`                                        -- Order s 12, step 1,200
    `a fine for failing to file a report, section 188`                     -- Order s 13, step 10
    -- the amounts of the s 120A "social deductions" list, and of "recognised donation amounts",
    -- for which the Order has no rule
    `an amount in section 9(16A), (16B) or (18A)`
    `the amount in section 17(5A)`
    `an amount in section 32(9) other than the grant of paragraph (a)(1)`
    `an amount in section 45A other than subsection (d)`
    `the amount in section 58A(c)`
    `an amount in section 125D`
    `a recognised donation amount, section 46(a)`

-- Fork R1. The Order is silent on the amounts above its thirteen; section 120B(d) says the Minister
-- "may" make rounding rules, and does not say what an amount is when he has not.
-- Ruled by Meng 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): one named switch, declined by default, the other reading kept.
DECLARE `A reading of an amount the Rounding Order has no rule for` IS ONE OF
    `the rounding of such an amount is declined`   -- the default
    `such an amount stays as adjusted`

